WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.360
<i>Ready... 1, 2, 3, GO!</i>

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.200
<i>Love life! Very! Very! Happy!</i>

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>Friendship life! Bouncing, jumping!</i>

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.710
<i>Adventure life! Heart-pounding, OK?</i>

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.670
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:28.300
<i>Rushing out onto the road to</i>
<i>school with the blue sky behind us</i>

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.260
<i>I like that! I like this, too!</i>

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.760
<i>I'll take it all, all of it~</i>

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>A girl who imagines love is all romance</i>

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.390
<i>If I can attack, I'll do it boldly</i>

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.020
<i>Let's find an original vision for the future</i>

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:49.940
<i>Sometimes, we'll have a secret love advice time</i>

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.780
<i>Who do you like?</i>

00:00:52.990 --> 00:01:00.330
<i>You've got a green light for love now!</i>
<i>It's your chance to move forward!</i>

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.160
<i>So, let's just</i>

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.170
<i>Have a blast! Fall in love!</i>

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.250
<i>Our youth is non-stop!</i>

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.340
<i>Run! Aim for the future!</i>

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.960
<i>Everyone gather</i>

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.840
<i>For a happy ending!</i>

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.390
<i>Will tomorrow be happy or sad?</i>
<i>Will we idle our time away?</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.470
<i>We'll work hard!</i>

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.770
<i>I want to keep dreaming forever!</i>

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.980
<i>Let's fly out into the</i>
<i>world with all our strength!</i>

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:28.860
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.280
Here I go!

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.570
Pyuru!

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.530
Got it!

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.910
Pyuru... pyu!

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:40.950
Huh?!

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.160
Cyan!

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.710
We're at a beach outside of Midi City right now.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.220
Are you all right, Cyan?

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.050
Sorry, pyuru!

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:00.560
We're at a training camp to write a new song
to perform at the Grateful Rock Festival.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.900
Are you okay?

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:14.440
Actually, we went through quite
an ordeal before getting to this point...

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.370
Um...

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.300
Ah, I can't take it anymore, darlings!

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.630
W-Wait... did the guitar just...

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.260
...say "darling"?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.050
You're worried about <i>that</i>, pyuru?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:47.020
This kid's completely depressed,
so I'll explain in her place.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.820
You all first met Cyan during
the Trichronika concert, right?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:59.490
We were able to make the dark monster
retreat with her guitar skills and my power.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.580
That image is probably
burned in all your minds, too.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:11.210
As long as we have Cyan's music skill,
we can defeat the dark monsters.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:16.380
Then, you were the one
who dragged her into this world?

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:24.510
No, the one who brought Cyan to Sound World
was the president of Unicorn Virtual Music,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.100
Dagger Morse!

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.640
Dagger Morse?!

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.610
By Dagger, you mean the bigwig
who controls the music world?!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:37.650
On top of that, he's from the
super major label that Grateful King,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:43.280
the only guitarist I respect, belongs to!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:50.370
However, he didn't drag Cyan
over here to fight monsters.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:55.920
Because Dagger's the one
controlling those dark monsters!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.050
His goal is money!

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.680
He's scheming to take all
of Sound World for himself.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.220
He plans to bring talented
musicians into his agency,

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:11.100
and erase all the rival bands
using dark monsters.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.980
In order to take over this world,
Dagger even looked to other worlds.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.570
That's where he zeroed in
on Cyan's guitar technique.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.490
Dagger found Cyan...?

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:30.040
He dragged her here forcibly to be
part of the ideal band he was creating.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.750
Well, I got in the way there, though.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.920
No way...!

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.800
And that's where I came in!

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:43.800
Then you knew all that when you
first asked Cyan to join Plasmagica?

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.350
Yes.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:50.020
So don't just blame Cyan. I am also at fault.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.060
Sorry, Chuchu.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:57.270
I wanted Cyan to increase
her music skill with you all

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.360
so that you could evolve
your Melodisians together.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:05.990
And then, you could save
this world from Dagger's evil.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.660
Why did you need to hide that from us?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.080
I didn't want you to have to carry
that burden from the beginning—

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.920
It was my parental love for you!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.460
You were thinking of us, President?

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.130
It wasn't because you just
missed your chance to tell them?

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.390
Stop dragging your feet!

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.930
That Dagger bastard's in
that tower over there, isn't he?

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.690
You should go straight there
and tell him off to his face!

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.600
All right! Let's teach him a lesson!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.820
No, no, you mustn't!
You mustn't do that, darlings!

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.690
"Darling"?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.160
Using brute force is no different
from using money to coerce people.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.950
Music is the only way
to beat that guy completely.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:53.710
We must...

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:54.830
...beat him...

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.040
...with music!

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.550
What is this? I'm getting super fired up!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.340
That doesn't matter right now!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.300
Huh?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.680
No matter what, you can't just
leave before a concert like that!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.390
I feel bad about that.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.610
However, Cyan was thinking of
the concert first, just like you guys.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.070
But I forced her to—

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.730
That's not it.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:28.320
I'm the one who couldn't talk to everyone
properly and who left before the concert.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.280
I'm the one to blame.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:37.250
I'm really sorry, Chuchu, Moa.
Even though it was an important concert...

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.340
It's fine, pyuru.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.130
I need to apologize to Retoree, too.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.430
But there's one thing I want
to make sure you understand.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:07:00.440
Plasmagica is really precious to me.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:04.940
I know that, pyuru! So does Chuchu, pyuru.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.910
I have decided!

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.620
Our agency will have a training camp!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:14.830
Training camp?!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.330
That's right! A training camp!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.170
Eating from the same pot—

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.130
Sleeping next to each other—

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.290
Speaking to each other without pretense—

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.840
An' erasin' all 'ard feelingsh
by spendin' time t'gether.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.220
Of course, we're not going for fun!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.390
The Grateful Rock Festival?!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.730
Isn't that the legendary rock festival?!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.150
Yes, that's right.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.480
Oh, legend!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.780
I'll have you write new songs
to present at this festival.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.360
We're leaving tomorrow!

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:53.410
Legend! Legend!

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.410
Well, where are we going, Prez?

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.370
Everyone knows that you have
training camp in the mountains!

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.500
Wait, what—?!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.590
A-Angelica, wh-where are we going?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.340
You'll find out eventually.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.230
The beach...

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.270
It's pretty, pyuru.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.870
Come now, work hard to push it, please.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.330
This is part of your training, too.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.540
Damn it, we'll use up all our strength
before we even get to the training camp!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.800
You can't give up with just this!

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.550
What Rom says is right.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.350
The more you complain,
the closer you are to being the weakest!

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.600
Hence—

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.350
Anyway, you push too, Wimpion!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:04.980
A divine evil god is whispering
in my ear, "You must not push."

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.280
I can't do this anymore...

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.530
You don't know anything, do you?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:16.700
Huh?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.750
The tough bodies created
from pushing as hard as you can

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.920
will bring our performance to greater heights!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:28.000
Don't waste a single second of this chance!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.340
That's right... That's right, Rom...!

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:37.930
The only guitarist I respect,
the legendary Grateful King, once said:

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.930
"When you're in trouble,
most of the time, it's a chance!"

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.980
I will go, to the Legend of the Other Side!

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:46.400
We are a team!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.520
If we put our strength together,
we can do anything!

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.030
I'll pick up your bones.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.990
Not pushin' yet?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.630
Oh...

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.600
Wow, this is amazing, pyuru!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.560
President...? Pyuru...?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.560
It's one of his relatives.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.860
They look exactly the same, pyuru.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:39.280
I'll be in the room next door,
so let me know if you need anything.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.510
Why don't I make some tea?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.800
There's fruit, too, pyuru.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.890
But it's almost time for dinner.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.270
I'm going to the hot tub.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.490
I'll go, too...

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.490
Then, I will too...

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.910
...I was thinking, but I'll go after dinner, pyuru!

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:28.500
Thanks, you two...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.500
I'll be back.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:43.140
Then... Then you have to go back someday?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.520
That's...

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.980
If you were going to go away,

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.730
then it would've been better
if you never came to begin with.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:57.900
Retoree...?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.650
Um...

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:17.300
I'm going to bare all and
tell you my feelings, okay?

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:24.800
I mean, this is a hot tub, so I'll bare all
since we're naked anyway! Just kidding...

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:33.150
I'm really sorry I didn't
say anything until now.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:37.820
I've loved playing guitar ever since I was little.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:42.240
I wrote songs and played them by myself.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:53.000
At first, I had enough fun just
playing and singing by myself...

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.460
...but when I heard the upperclassmen play,

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.380
it made me want to be in a band someday, too.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:08.140
But I didn't have the courage to join the band,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.770
so when I came here and
everyone asked me to join,

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.150
I was really happy.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.650
Hey, Retoree, you know what?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:28.030
I wish I could've told you this sooner.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:34.080
Even though everyone in
Plasmagica is truly precious to me...

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.020
Is Retoree still mad, pyuru?

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.480
I think she's more sad than angry.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:03.030
She's sad that you'll go back
to your own world someday, Cyan.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.660
"Own world," pyuru...?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.240
Even if that's the case, Moa and I are here,

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:13.910
so the two of us need to get closer to Retoree.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.540
Pyururururu...

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.250
What do you mean by "almost there," Rom?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.760
Rom! Have we not completely lost
the path we should be following? Hence—

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:28.590
We're lost in an infinite hell where we
won't even reach the oracle, aren't we?

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:33.270
How am I supposed to know, dimwits?
What about you guys—

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.270
Prez?

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.070
Yer terrible bastards fer runnin'
wild in my huntin' grounds!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.490
M-M-M-M-My hair...! My hair!

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.490
Please excuse me for
bothering you at this busy time.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.700
Here is my business card.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.040
Whaddaya want...?

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.870
You don't have to be suspicious of us.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:15:01.000
Actually, we were separated from the
rest of our party, and have lost our way.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.630
I suppose we should be impressed
by the guy with a real job.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.970
City boys, huh? Come wi' me.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.510
What do you want to do?

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.970
Grateful King said this, too:

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:17.690
"When you meet a hunter in the mountains,
most of the time, they're good guys."

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:23.520
Can we really trust this
man's character and King's jokes?

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.360
Yer hungry, aren't ya?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:57.180
♪ Counting the lights of the stars quietly ♪

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:04.690
♪ Hiding my sorrow ♪

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.490
♪ Have you noticed? ♪

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:17.580
♪ Just thinking about you makes my heart hurt ♪

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:22.120
♪ I can't sleep ♪

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.750
♪ Nights like this ♪

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:33.970
♪ Oh, just let me have one wish ♪

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:42.770
♪ Falling star of dreams
shining in the night sky ♪

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:50.150
♪ I want to see it from the same place as you ♪

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:55.410
♪ No matter how far apart we are ♪

00:16:55.620 --> 00:17:05.130
♪ Our hearts will one day become one ♪

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.260
Hey, Cyan, you said it before, didn't you?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.550
That with your bandmates,

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:20.810
you can understand each other
better with music than with words.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.770
That really is true.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.940
I can accept your feelings if you want.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.320
No, I <i>will</i> accept them.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:33.860
Retoree...!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.700
Thanks, meow!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.250
Is this case closed then, darlings?

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.040
You're floating...

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.750
You're speaking effeminately again?

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.960
Will you please not mess
around at times like this?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.380
I'm not messing around!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:52.210
I'm such a cute guitar,
so I can sound girlish if I want, darling!

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.680
Speaking of which...

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.550
Where's Moa?

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.520
What should I do, pyuru?

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:06.810
I can't say anything after all this time, pyuru.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.480
Don't be rash!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.270
Pyuru?

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.480
What's the matter, Moa?

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:17.200
There's something I've been
hiding from everyone, pyuru.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.250
I, Moa, will make an important
announcement right now, pyuru!

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.880
O-Okay, please calm down!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:32.920
I am... The real me is...

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:39.390
An alien from another planet who was
ordered to investigate this planet, pyuru!

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:41.060
Huh?

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:45.310
Wait, come on. In a band with just
four people, isn't it a little too gimmicky

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.900
for one of them to be from another
world and another to be an alien?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:52.230
I think it's Moa's way
of making Cyan feel better.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.570
Thanks, Moa! But everything's fine now!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.660
It's true, pyuru!

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.200
Wait just a minute!

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.580
Can't we use this "too gimmicky" gimmick?

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:04.700
A band with an alien and
a person from another world!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.580
Oh, then the two of us should have gimmicks, too!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.670
They aren't planning on believing me, pyuru?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:12.710
In that case—

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:15.420
Pyurururu-rururu!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.010
What?!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:25.220
Moa!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.200
I couldn't tell you two, either, pyuru.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.880
So Retoree, please don't
just blame Cyan, pyuru...

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.290
That's not an issue anymore!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:59.340
Anyway, the four of us are bandmates right now.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:02.510
We should enjoy that to the fullest.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.720
It doesn't matter if you're
an alien or from another world.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:10.440
We just want to treasure this
time we have together right now.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.440
That's how it is.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.570
Yeah!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.780
Everyone! You're the best, pyuru!

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:20.200
Huh?

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.990
Moa...

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.330
Sorry, pyuru...

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.000
We made good use of our
first day at training camp, huh?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.080
Yeah.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:40.090
Everyone, why don't we brush up that
song we just sang and make it our new song?

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.840
Huh?!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.680
Really?

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:48.850
And I'd like Cyan to sing
vocals with me on this song.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.890
M-Me?!

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:57.860
Ever since I first heard you sing,
I've wanted to sing together.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:01.780
I wonder if I can sing in front of people...

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.740
I think you can.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.280
I do too, pyuru!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:07.580
Thanks!

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:11.370
Now, since we're playing
at the Grateful Rock Festival,

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:16.040
I want to leave an impression
so people remember Plasmagica!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.540
Yeah!

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.720
And so, our training camp began.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.560
Well, take care.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:32.310
Thanks. We owe you one, old man.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.310
Real rock!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:39.280
Grateful King...!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:44.660
I'm gonna make the greatest
song the same way you did!

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:46.820
Why must I do this with you?

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.080
I don't know...!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.870
You're all fired up.

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:03.010
<i>If you like it, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.880
<i>You can do it because you like it</i>

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.600
<i>The feeling that you like music</i>

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.970
<i>Can't be stopped by anyone</i>

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:22.610
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:26.160
<i>Running through my body</i>

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>This electric thrill</i>

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:33.700
<i>Is this feeling curiosity?</i>

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:37.250
<i>Negativity is a decrescendo</i>

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:39.920
<i>Hope and expectations, a crescendo</i>

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:45.470
<i>Show off our passion and</i>
<i>get god to be our ally, too</i>

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:50.970
<i>I wanna share with everyone and have a taste of</i>

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:54.680
<i>Big!! Rocking!! Heart-throbbing!! Happiness!!!!</i>

00:22:55.680 --> 00:22:58.730
<i>If it's you, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:01.730
<i>You can do it because it's you</i>

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:06.820
<i>Let's try performing these</i>
<i>dream-colored notes together</i>

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:10.030
<i>I want to tell you directly</i>

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:12.870
<i>A life-sized, "heart-sized" heart</i>

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.750
<i>In order for it to reach you...</i>

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:19.080
<i>I will sing with all I have</i>

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.840
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.800
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:29.180
In Midi City, there are places where
not even I have stepped foot. Hence—

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:33.100
You should try going to Yokai Street once.
Let's try it! It's a devilish mystery!

00:23:33.310 --> 00:23:35.180
A mysterious devil from the world of spirits?

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:38.310
Is it finally time for this
sun of darkness to take action?

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:39.650
You've got to seize the chance!
